request.description:
Returns the preprocessed image that Tesseract actually receives (as base64 JPEG).

Use this to diagnose OCR failures — copy the image_b64 from the response and decode it to see if the image quality/contrast is good enough.

Quick decode in browser console:
  const img = document.createElement('img');
  img.src = 'data:image/jpeg;base64,' + response.image_b64;
  document.body.appendChild(img);
